KNOWNBUG
main.ii
--winx64
^\[handler\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ terminate called from the unwinding: SUCCESS$
^\[handler\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
no body for callee
--
With the MSVC runtime, set_terminate was not modelled (it is extern "C",
named `set_terminate', not `std::set_terminate(...)'), and the call of
the terminate handler on an escaping exception looked up only
`std::terminate()': cpp11_terminate_when_destructor_throws_during_unwinding
failed on VS 2022 ("no body for callee set_terminate").  The runtime's
terminate, set_terminate and _get_terminate are now modelled.
